WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.563
Chapter 05 adds two things.

2
00:00:02.563 --> 00:00:03.800
The first is a guard.

3
00:00:03.800 --> 00:00:08.188
The client already skipped a record whose
intended state was completely empty.

4
00:00:08.188 --> 00:00:12.039
But it didn't skip one that was a
non-empty object naming nothing,

5
00:00:12.039 --> 00:00:16.113
with empty attributes and an empty
list of entitlements to remove.

6
00:00:16.113 --> 00:00:19.029
That's exactly what the
script stores for a native

7
00:00:19.029 --> 00:00:22.088
change the workflow didn't
describe, the Module 5 gap.

8
00:00:22.088 --> 00:00:24.736
Comparing any read with it always matches,

9
00:00:24.736 --> 00:00:29.050
so the client would have closed that
record, with evidence, on nothing.

10
00:00:29.050 --> 00:00:33.440
Now, before reading anything, the
client checks the intended state, and a

11
00:00:33.440 --> 00:00:38.350
record that names nothing checkable is
skipped with the reason, never verified.

12
00:00:38.350 --> 00:00:40.425
The second is an offline mode.

13
00:00:40.425 --> 00:00:44.124
It takes saved waiting records,
saved reads and a fixed clock,

14
00:00:44.124 --> 00:00:47.675
and makes the same decisions
with only the reader swapped.

15
00:00:47.675 --> 00:00:51.380
It's a dry run only; the
apply option is refused.
